FILED s521d (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-18) from the #3516 probes (scratch/s521d/pr/g2.pl in the s521d worktree).
    sub via_arg { my $rval = \$_[0]; return "" . $$rval }
    my $l = bless \do { local *FH }, 'W'; print via_arg($$l), "\n";
perl 5.40.3: `*main::FH`.  PCL (68aeebf5 and the s521d tree alike): `*main::FH__PCL_LOCAL_1` -- the glob a `local *FH` makes is named by the lowering's internal rename, and that name leaks into the glob's stringification (and so into Data::Dump of an `\do { local *FH }` handle).  PRE-EXISTING; LOW.  Fix shape: the localized glob keeps the Perl name it localizes (`*main::FH`) as its display name; the internal symbol stays internal.
